# Differential test of number-arrays.js: arrays of Numbers that map makes
# are std::vector<ctnative::js_num>, and Number.parseInt and Math.min call
# ctnative::Number.parseInt and ctnative::Math.min. The C++ is compiled
# against public Core, checked for interpreter symbols with nm, run, and
# every global compared with the interpreter's (compilation-unit.py). The
# negative changes the global `offsets` and requires the comparison to fail
# naming it. compile-clean.py checks a warning-free build on both
# toolchains. string-arrays-calls.py is the generic pipeline driver for a
# fixture that is not registered in NativeFixtures.cmake.

# RUN: python3 %S/string-arrays-calls.py --translate ctjs-translate --opt ctjs-opt --js %S/number-arrays.js --out %t/number-arrays.emitc.mlir
# RUN: ctjs-translate --mlir-to-cpp %t/number-arrays.emitc.mlir | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %compilation_unit --module %t/number-arrays.emitc.mlir --js %S/number-arrays.js --work %t --name number_arrays --core-build %build
# RUN: not %compilation_unit --module %t/number-arrays.emitc.mlir --js %S/number-arrays.js --work %t --name number_arrays_negative --core-build %build --mutate offsets 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NEGATIVE
# RUN: %compile_clean --module %t/number-arrays.emitc.mlir --work %t --name number_arrays

# CHECK-DAG: std::vector<ctnative::js_num>
# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::Number.parseInt(
# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::Math.min(
# CHECK-DAG: ctnative::Array.prototype.map.call(
# NEGATIVE: global 'offsets' differs
